{"conjecture": "The set of behaviors covered by a test suite exhibits diminishing returns: each new test covers an incrementally smaller marginal fraction of the system's possible execution states, because the space of interactions is not submodular with respect to coverage. While each individual change adds a locally correct, well-tested feature, the residual uncovered interaction space grows combinatorially, so future modifications increasingly perturb behaviors that no existing test exercises. This submodular deficit means the test suite’s marginal protective value per change decays even as total coverage percentage rises, creating an expanding shadow of untested interactions that makes every future change riskier and harder to reason about."}
